A Russian cargo ship caught fire after ​being hit by drones in the Baltic Sea on Saturday and drifted into Finnish waters. Reporting from Kyiv, FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg notes that the ship is affiliated with a major Russian military logistics company. While Ukrainian authorities typically neither confirm nor deny responsibility, analysts cite a clear motive for the targeting, Cragg explains. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8752a08e-e5d2-11f1-bad2-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-180424-180619-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8752a08e-e5d2-11f1-bad2-e56ab3dc0809/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-180424-180619-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8ce73186-e5d2-11f1-a09a-734ccf1eac6b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 18:02:23 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>COP31: Deep divisions persist over energy, finance and science</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/cop31-deep-divisions-persist-over-energy-finance-and-science</link><description>
COP31 climate talks in Turkey have gone into overtime, with deep divisions over fossil fuels, climate finance and global warming targets delaying an agreement. A revised draft dropped all mention of fossil fuels, prompting strong criticism from the EU and a dozen countries demanding a clear commitment to phase them out. Negotiators are also split over a proposed global electrification target, carbon capture and the future of UN climate science reports. Developing nations have voiced anger over the removal of a $120 billion climate adaptation funding target. Australia is now racing to secure a revised deal before delegates leave. France 24 journalist Adria Rocha Cutiller tells us the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e281d9c-e5d0-11f1-9a79-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-171141-171326-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2e281d9c-e5d0-11f1-9a79-6b451f569414/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-171141-171326-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3399d0d6-e5d0-11f1-94aa-0152d9761961</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:26:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>FBI criminal database hacked</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/fbi-criminal-database-hacked</link><description>
The FBI is investigating a reported major cyberattack targeting its national law enforcement database, the National Crime Information Center (NCIC), which holds sensitive criminal justice records, including information on fugitives, missing persons, criminal histories and stolen property. President Donald Trump said he had just been briefed on the incident, describing it as “not good”. FRANCE 24’s Fraser Jackson reports from Washington DC.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24146280-e5cf-11f1-94fc-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-170210-170558-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24146280-e5cf-11f1-94fc-13439ca2fe89/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261121-170210-170558-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">28e3e812-e5cf-11f1-a731-ad576a554f7c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:23:18 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Man convicted of starting palisades fire</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/man-convicted-of-starting-palisades-fire</link><description>
A Los Angeles County jury found former rideshare driver Jonathan Rinderknecht guilty on Friday of starting the 2025 Palisades fire, which caused widespread destruction and loss of life. He faces a prison sentence of between five and 40 years. Liza Kaminov has more.
